  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 109 PM CDT Fri Oct 30 2026\n\nUpper level ridge briefly moves across the area for Saturday night\nand Sunday, but will be watching the next potent system for the\nPlains for Monday and Tuesday. Models are having their struggle\nwith this system, but it appears very dynamic as it tries to close\noff and move across Oklahoma and North Texas. Still questionable\nwhether any of the main lift with this system will be far enough\nsouth to impact West Central Texas, but in any case, it will be\nsurging a cold front through the area. With moisture still in\nplace, this front will have some CAPE to work with and some\nshowers and storms will remain possible. Best rain chances will be\nacross the Heartland and Hill Country Monday Night and Tuesday\nmorning as the front reaches the moisture. CAMs will have a better\nhandle on this event over the weekend, so wont mess with the blend\nPOPs at this point. Of note, SPC does have the northern Big\nCountry in a Day 4 Slight Risk of severe storms for Monday\nafternoon/evening.\n\nCold front drops through the area and brings cooler and drier\nconditions to West Central Texas for mid/end of next week. Lows \nin the 40s, highs in the 70s.",
